# Snyk policy file.
# No `expires:` field is set on the ignore below: the rationale is
# structural (the attack surface does not exist for a Terraform
# provider), so a periodic re-review would only re-confirm the same
# conclusion.
version: v1.0.0
ignore:
  SNYK-GOLANG-GITHUBCOMVMIHAILENCOMSGPACKV5-15702238:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-2454 in github.com/vmihailenco/msgpack/v5 v5.4.1.
          The advisory describes the attack vector as "websocket messages
          containing malformed msgpack frames" causing excessive memory
          consumption and a server crash. This Terraform provider does
          not accept untrusted msgpack input over a network: msgpack is
          used only inside the gRPC plugin protocol between the trusted
          Terraform CLI parent process and this provider. The described
          attack surface does not apply.

          The provider's use of msgpack is mediated entirely by the
          Terraform plugin gRPC protocol; we do not parse arbitrary
          msgpack from any other source, and there is no path by which
          a network attacker could deliver a malformed msgpack frame to
          this binary. This is a structural property of how Terraform
          providers run, so the conclusion is not expected to change.
        created: 2026-04-30
